+# Additional LINE channels (distinct Developers Console bot registrations)
+# for this same gateway process — NOT representable via env, unlike every
+# knob above. Set as a structured list under `platforms.line.extra.channels`
+# in config.yaml, e.g.:
+#
+#   platforms:
+#     line:
+#       extra:
+#         channels:
+#           - profile: coder            # must match an existing gateway
+#                                        # profile name; "default" is reserved
+#             channel_access_token: "..."
+#             channel_secret: "..."
+#             allowed_users: ["Uxxxxxxxx"]
+#             dm_policy: pairing        # optional, defaults to "pairing"
+#
+# Each additional channel gets its own webhook route
+# (/line/p/<profile>/webhook — the default channel keeps the unprefixed
+# /line/webhook unchanged) and its own allowlists/dm_policy, fully isolated
+# from every other configured channel. Register that URL as that channel's
+# webhook endpoint in its own LINE Developers Console entry.
+# See modules/line/line_multiplex.py and plans/line-multi-channel-plan.md
+# in the hermes-render repo for the full design.
